      "side": 1,
      "message": "I always thought `@VisibleForTesting` was unneccessary for public because that\u0027s already the highest visibility. When I saw the usage in this class, I looked at the docs and found:\n\n\u003e Do not use this [`@VisibleForTesting`] interface for public or protected declarations: it is a fig leaf for bad design, and it does not prevent anyone from using the declaration and experience has shown that they will\n\nhttp://google3/third_party/java_src/google_common/current/java/com/google/common/annotations/VisibleForTesting.java;l\u003d21;rcl\u003d622629825\n\nBut searching cs for `@VisibleForTesting public` does yield thousands and thousands of results. So now I am not sure.",
      "parentUuid": "9de57174_e1b972aa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "9bacf837d2122018d4da79bca4153a77e33b40e9",
